{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778904988,"nonce":"GPMSNkZyehK2OJCFwKh6L5vApd8=","title":"Graph view filters and layout are not inspection-ready","message":"The current Graph view has several blocking inspection issues:\n\n- Repo/branch filters use single-selection combobox behavior that looks and behaves poorly for the intended multi-select workflow.\n- Mode counts are global while the rendered graph and layer counts are filtered/capped, which makes counts look inconsistent after repo selection.\n- Filtered activity graphs can drop session layers entirely when there are no matching session nodes; this is accurate data-wise but needs clearer filter/count semantics.\n- The React Flow layout currently stacks nodes in one or two vertical columns, causing edges to overlap and making the graph hard to read.\n\nFix should keep complex issue cross-reference indexing out of scope unless explicitly approved, and should focus on immediate UI clarity: polished multi-select filters, honest visible/total counts, and a more readable graph layout.\n\nBug: de2f8ac\nBug: 78af187","files":null}]}